					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wrongjohnsilver" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2000367); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2000367&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607374201" alt="WrongJohnSilver" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2000367)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wrongjohnsilver" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2000367); return false;" >WrongJohnSilver</a></span> <span class="odate time_1445273394 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Oct 2015 16:49</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2393891">
									

<p>I definitely recommend reading and comparing <a href="/scp-2598">the Moth Helmet</a>. The basic idea of a box that does nothing more than make you left-handed isn't bad, in and of itself, and the item doesn't have to be particularly useful (it's actually a bit more interesting because it isn't). However, as it stands, the object begins and ends with just the pun, and that's not enough to carry the story.</p>
<p>Some possible ways to expand on it:</p>
<ul>
<li>Why would a box that makes you left-handed exist?</li>
<li>Did someone get the definition of &quot;sinister&quot; wrong in its development?</li>
<li>Did someone get the definition of &quot;sinister&quot; right in its development?</li>
<li>Why is it so hammy?</li>
<li>What happens if it's powered by a deasil engine instead of a AA battery?</li>
</ul>
<p>It doesn't need to be long (and probably best if it's short). But we need more than just the one pun.</p>

							</div>

								
