			<div class="content" id="post-content-2394053">
									

<p>It is the origin of right=good, left=bad symbolism (&quot;Left Hand of Darkness&quot;, &quot;Red Right Hand&quot; &quot;Right Hand Man&quot;). Also found in heraldry (&quot;Bar Sinister<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-820187-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-820187-1')">1</a></sup>&quot;, &quot;Lion Dexter Argent&quot;) which definitely appear in <em>A Song of Ice and Fire</em> (the TV version of which I gather is somewhat popular), the words &quot;ambidextrous&quot;, &quot; dexterous&quot;, &quot;dexterity&quot; and &quot;sinister&quot;, Mr. Sinister in Marvel comics and Jeff Lindsay's eponymous &quot;good&quot; serial killer Dexter Morgan. Also as I said the funk band Sinister Dexter, and the British comic book <em>Sinister Dexter</em>.</p>
<p>ETA- also the &quot;dex&quot; in pre-IUPAC names for things like dextrose and dextroamphetimine.</p>
