			<div class="content" id="post-content-2394881">
									

<p>Siding with the pudding here: sinister &amp; dexter really are two of the basic latin words everyone should know; if they don't, well here's their chance to learn.</p>
<p>On a side note, sinister meaning evil didn't come about the way a lot of people think- the original secondary meaning was that if you were doing something sinister, you were working in a cunning and subtle way. Its only during the era of (hypothetical) chivalry that &quot;using intelligent tactics/strategy&quot; and &quot;dirty cheater&quot; became conflated, and being sinister was suddenly a bad thing.</p>

